    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d909">

                <pb facs="0817" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg645"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.55/8</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitlock</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-26T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>257. To be considered in connection with Department’s telegram of to-day
                    regarding Belgian relief:</p>
                <p>You and the consuls should postpone your departure from Belgium until you are
                    officially assured by German authorities that all Americans who wish to leave
                    Belgium may do so without hindrance. You should advise all Americans to leave
                    and facilitate their departure. This of course does not apply to members of
                    relief commission until further instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
